      "content": "$MEME 1H The closing price of the 1D cycle has just broken above the 10-day high. Currently, the price is hovering around 0.0006, and the bullish momentum is in a volume-expansion breakout, with a strong “volume burst” state. In terms of the moving average structure, although the price has moved above the three lines, the overall trend alignment has not been fully confirmed yet, and the tug-of-war between bulls and bears remains intense. Given that the volume has clearly expanded to 3.10x average volume and the local structure has not gone out of control, look one line higher directly.\n{future}(MEMEUSDT)\nTrading Plan—Go Long📈:\nEntry: 0.000585 – 0.000587\nStop Loss: 0.000525\nFirst Target: 0.000678\nSecond Target: 0.000739\nThird Target: 0.000830\nWhy choose this setup?\n• A breakout with 3.10x average volume—this is a very strong signal of capital entering\n• EMA144 support is at 0.000526; if it breaks, we admit defeat—defense level is easy to define\n• RSI tops out at 74.2, indicating the bullish charge momentum is still expanding\n• The price’s first time standing above the three moving averages is a standard trend-entry point\n🚨 Market Reminder\nAlthough price has surged into the new high range around 0.0006, the bigger environment is actually more inclined toward consolidation, not a one-direction, nonstop bull run. EMA144, EMA169, and EMA233 are all crowded near 0.0005; the current deviation is already 11.56%. Chasing at the high without restraint isn’t a great trade-off.\n📌 Key Levels\nThe most critical “do-not-break” line below is 0.000525—this is also the dense support zone of the moving-average cluster. On the upside, the first resistance to watch is 0.000678. Only if it can enter the trade area and hold there with volume should we look to test higher targets of 0.000739 and 0.000830.\n👀 Next to Watch\nThe biggest question now is that the moving averages have not fully spread out yet. Next, watch whether the 1H candle can close above 0.000585. If the bulls can consolidate here on reduced volume and shake out the market, that would be the most ideal “building strength” condition.\n⚠️ Technical analysis is for reference only and does not constitute investment advice👇👇👇\n#BTC #ETH $BTC $ETH \n{future}(BTCUSDT)\n{future}(ETHUSDT)",
